  "_why": "3.6: Ensnaring Strike's 10-round ceiling. The restraint is a shared condition now, with no round of its own; the spell's last round (ensnaring_expires_round, cast round + 9 = 10) ends the concentration, and that clears the restraint. The round is moved on to 11 before the enemy's turn: the vines are gone before it acts, so it takes no thorn damage and makes no Strength check, and concentration is none. The low roll on that turn would fail the check if the vines still held.",
